//
// Normative rule menvcfg_stce_zero_op (src/priv/machine.adoc):
//   When this extension is implemented and STCE in menvcfg is zero, an attempt to access stimecmp
//     or vstimecmp in a mode other than M-mode raises an illegal-instruction exception, STCE in
//     henvcfg is read-only zero, and STIP in mip and sip reverts to its defined behavior as if this
//     extension is not implemented.
//
// Context:
//   Without Sstc, mip.STIP is writable by M-mode, which uses it to deliver supervisor timer
//     interrupts (mip_stip_no_stimecmp_acc, mip_stip_no_stimecmp_mmode_write); sip.STIP is read-
//     only.
//
// Clarifications:
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/1636: when STCE changes, mip.STIP/sip.STIP
//     takes an UNSPECIFIED value (the CSR field-modulation rule, quoted by ved-rivos): "If a write
//     to one CSR changes the set of legal values allowed for a field of a second CSR ... the second
//     CSR's field immediately gets an UNSPECIFIED value from among its new legal values." Tests
//     write mip.STIP after clearing STCE before relying on it.
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/3329: the STCE=0 rule covers "stimecmp or
//     vstimecmp"; the vstimecmp words were restored after an accidental drop.
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/1312: writes to the read-only henvcfg.STCE are
//     ignored.
//
// Test plan:
//   1. With STCE=0 and mcounteren.TM swept over 0 and 1: every CSR instruction form on stimecmp in
//     S-mode raises illegal-instruction (xtval 0 or the instruction bits); on RV32 also stimecmph;
//     reads and writes from U-mode do too.
//   2. M-mode (T-SBI) accesses still work: a write of a random value reads back.
//   3. STIP reverts: M-mode sets and clears mip.STIP, and sip.STIP follows, with stimecmp at 0 and
//     at all ones (the comparison no longer drives STIP).
//   4. The reverted STIP still drives interrupts: with sstatus.SIE=1 and sie.STIE=1, no interrupt
//     while mip.STIP=0 and stimecmp=0; an interrupt once M-mode sets mip.STIP.
//   5. sip.STIP stays read-only from S-mode with STCE=0: csrrs/csrrc of sip do not flip it.
//   6. With H: henvcfg.STCE was 1 before menvcfg.STCE was cleared and must now read 0, and still
//     reads 0 after HS-mode tries to set it; HS-mode access to vstimecmp and VS-mode access to
//     stimecmp (henvcfg/hcounteren enabled) raise illegal-instruction, not virtual-instruction.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 12293
//

